8.1 Demo Video Requirements
The submission must include a screen-recorded demonstration with voice-over covering: project name, purpose, use and benefits, working process, and final output. Uploaded to Google Drive, link set to Anyone with the link can view.

8.2 Demo Script (5 minutes)
The form (30s). Point out the five fields and that a non-artist can fill this in with no tooling knowledge.
Generate a comic (90s — narrate over the wait). Use the fox/enchanted-forest prompt. Explain while it runs: outline first, then narration, then five illustrations.
Walk the preview page (60s). Take one panel and show its four layers — title, image, italic scene description, caption and narration — plus the image-prompt reference shown for transparency.
Iterate on tone (60s). Resubmit the same premise with funny + comic book. Show the visible difference. This is the strongest part of the demo: it proves the pipeline genuinely re-runs rather than re-skinning.
Export (45s). Click download, show the PDF opening with one panel per page, land on the success page.
Show /docs (30s). Demonstrate /generate-comic/json and /test-image, making the point that the same engine is API-accessible.
8.3 Demo Preparation Checklist
One pre-generated PDF open in a second window, in case the live diffusion run is slow on the demo machine.
API keys confirmed working before recording.
Test microphone level and screen resolution before the take.
Close notifications.
